# VG-RASTER (VIRT-GEOM step 12/13): the cluster cut's clusters are HARDWARE-rastered through the material cells (each
# opaque Static group's `.Binned.VirtualGeometry` permutation) into the main pass, and the VG instances are out of the
# main view's bins. Project: F:/BistroFoliageProj. UNVERIFIED (written unbuilt): the lantern import repeats
# VIRT-GEOM-COOK.scn's first steps; the camera is VIRT-GEOM-COOK's [vg_cut] near position.
# The "bins-only" reference frames: the same steps on commit 92fbdd55d (VG instances drawn by the bins).
# Step 14: per-cut-view candidate regions (each view's cut dispatch covers only its own candidates), the post
# phase's carried clusters packed 64 per workgroup, cascade cuts LOD by the cascade's own texel size.
# Step 13: post phase (a cluster the previous frame's HZB hid is re-cut against this frame's HZB and drawn by the
# GBuffer post pass) and the shadow cascades' own cuts (VG instances out of the cascade bins too).
Дано run Scene "Open Scene Bistro.desce"
Когда run Assets "Drop into the viewport: Meshes/Bistro/Bistro_Exterior_Lantern.fbx"
Когда run Assets "Import Options: Virtual Geometry On"
Когда run Assets "Import Options: Import"
Когда run View "View mode: Lit"
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position -800,190,-60
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.6,-0.17,0.78
Когда 60 frames render
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position 300,190,400
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction -0.6,-0.17,-0.78
Когда 1 frames render
Когда shot viewport "vg_raster_cut60.png"
Когда 59 frames render
Когда DesertCtl state views.virtualGeometry
Тогда [vg_raster] views.virtualGeometry.instances >= 1, binnedVgInstances == 0 (main AND cascade views: every cull view has a cut view), clustersDrawn > 0, shadowClustersDrawn > 0 (the sun's cascades draw the lantern's clusters), overflow 0
Тогда [vg_raster] editor.log: 0 VUID, no "[MeshRenderer] ... has no `.VirtualGeometry` pipeline" for the lantern's cell, no "the view draws no virtual geometry this frame", no "occluded entries past the post carry's capacity"
Тогда-вид [vg_raster] vg_raster_cut60.png (the frame right after the camera cut, where last frame's HZB is of the other camera): no missing cluster - pixel diff vs the bins-only frame of the same steps < 1% of pixels (pixel diff, not thumbnails)
Тогда-вид [vg_raster] the lit frame at frame 120 shows the lantern and its shadow as in the bins-only frame: frame mean within 1%
Тогда [vg_raster_views] (step 14: candidates compacted per cut view, post clusters 64 per workgroup, cascade LOD by the cascade's own texel) vg_raster_cut60.png differs from the bins-only frame by < 1% of pixels; views.virtualGeometry.clustersDrawn > 0 and shadowClustersDrawn > 0; editor.log 0 VUID
Тогда [vg_vsm] (step 16: the VSM clipmap levels are cluster cut views, their clusters rastered into the pages; Shadows.Method VirtualMaps, Bistro, 120 frames) views.virtualGeometry.vsmClustersDrawn[level] > 0 on every level that drew pages; the sun shadow (lit frame 120) differs from the bins-only VSM frame by < 1% of pixels (pixel diff); editor.log 0 VUID, no "the virtual shadow map draws its virtual geometry on the CPU walk"
# Step 18/19 [vg_vsm_mixed]: a MIXED primitive - VG clusters on some submeshes only - casts into the VSM from BOTH parts.
# UNVERIFIED SETUP: a cooked mesh carries a DAG on every submesh or none (VirtualMeshTable.cpp:276-288, import gate
# VirtualGeometryGate.cpp:62-90), so the mix exists only per entry: a lantern section whose slot material is swapped
# (Details) to a template without a `.VirtualGeometry` twin stays on the levels' CPU walk (MeshRenderer::VsmWalkHidden)
# while its other sections are clustered. That section is a held refusal (vsmRefusedGroups counts it) - the step
# below states 0 per the brief; the agent that runs it names the setup that gives a twin-less group no refusal or
# changes the expected count (REMAINDER-VIRT-GEOM-19 item 3).
Когда run Scene "Set Shadows Method: VirtualMaps"
Когда 120 frames render
Когда shot viewport "vg_vsm_mixed120.png"
Когда DesertCtl state views.virtualGeometry
Тогда [vg_vsm_mixed] views.virtualGeometry.vsmClustersDrawn: one entry per clipmap level (17), > 0 on every level that drew pages (named per level in the report); views.virtualGeometry.vsmRefusedGroups == 0
Тогда [vg_vsm_mixed] editor.log: 0 VUID, no "has no `.VirtualGeometry` twin", no "the virtual shadow map draws its virtual geometry on the CPU walk"
Тогда-вид [vg_vsm_mixed] vg_vsm_mixed120.png: the lantern's shadow holds BOTH its clustered (metal frame) and walked (glass/masked) parts - pixel diff of the shadow vs the bins-only VSM frame of the same steps < 1% of pixels (pixel diff, not thumbnails)
Когда run Scene "Set Shadows Method: Cascades"
Когда 2 frames render
Когда DesertCtl state views.virtualGeometry
Тогда [vg_vsm_mixed] after switching back to cascades: views.virtualGeometry.vsmRefusedGroups == 0 (reset every frame the method is not VirtualMaps)
Когда run View "View mode: Virtual Geometry Clusters"
Тогда-вид [vg_raster] the lantern shows per-cluster colours on the same silhouette as the lit frame
